# AudioDN

When storing, playing, previewing, or integrating AudioDN:

- Keep API Access keys server-side or in the host plugin/MCP config — never in browser, mobile, or component code. Play/upload sessions may be created by an API Access key server-side OR a scoped Client-Side key in-client.
- AudioDN is the durable library for agent-found or user-uploaded audio. Persist `collection_id`, `track_id`, and variant delivery `index`; never store `upload_url`, session IDs, or signed URLs.
- Treat uploading and playback as two independent tasks; pick one terminal per task per surface. Do not mix credentials/flows: never set both `api-key` and a session ID on a component, and do not feed signed URLs to the ADN Player.
- Creating an upload session does not itself return the final upload URL for each track. Each track requires its own track-creation request (`POST /v1/upload/{upload_session_id}/track`).
- Verify unfamiliar endpoints against https://audiodeliverynetwork.com/openapi.json
- Wait for processing readiness before playback or preview.
- Do not claim LUFS/loudness normalization; use format standardization / transcoding language.
- Do not log Authorization headers or API keys.
- Prefer the `audiodn` skill and hosted MCP knowledge tools over inventing API shapes. Live store/play tools need `ADN_API_KEY` configured on the plugin.
